      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] 💡 **Minor Suggestion:** Consider adding `__attribute__((weak))` to these `extern` declarations:\n\n```c\n__attribute__((weak)) extern uint32_t __ahb4_start[];\n__attribute__((weak)) extern uint32_t __ahb4_end[];\n```\n\nWhile this currently works for all existing STM32H7 boards that define the `.ahb4` region, making these symbols weak prevents linker errors if a new STM32H7 board is added in the future that does *not* define `.ahb4` in its `memory_regions.inc`. If undefined, weak symbols resolve to `0`, and your `if ((uintptr_t)__ahb4_end \u003e (uintptr_t)__ahb4_start)` check on line 308 will safely evaluate to false and skip the `memset`.",
